@host = http://localhost:5091
# Needed by /api/documents/extract once Auth:ApiKeys is configured (always, outside Development).
@apiKey = 

### Liveness (200 whenever the process is up)
GET {{host}}/health/live

### Readiness (503 while models load; 200 Degraded if one failed to load)
GET {{host}}/health/ready

### Negative feedback
POST {{host}}/api/feedback/analyze
Content-Type: application/json

{ "text": "The room was filthy, the staff were rude and the noise kept us up all night. Never again." }

### Positive feedback
POST {{host}}/api/feedback/analyze
Content-Type: application/json

{ "text": "Wonderful stay! Friendly staff, spotless room, great breakfast." }

### Mixed feedback
POST {{host}}/api/feedback/analyze
Content-Type: application/json

{ "text": "Lovely location but the room was tiny and the wifi barely worked." }

### Invalid (400)
POST {{host}}/api/feedback/analyze
Content-Type: application/json

{ "text": "" }

### Extract fields from a UCC-1 (needs an OpenAI key: the Extraction:ApiKey user secret or OPENAI_API_KEY; 503 without one)
POST {{host}}/api/documents/extract
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=docintake

--docintake
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="redwood-mechanical-ucc1-fax.pdf"
Content-Type: application/pdf

< ../../docs/samples/pdf/corpus/redwood-mechanical-ucc1-fax.pdf
--docintake--
